{
  "$comment": [
    "Reference data for the academic calendar, migrated from the legacy",
    "db/db_data/academic_structure.json.",
    "",
    "Data, not code: adding a grade or a term must not require editing a seed",
    "script. The legacy system learned this the hard way — its first seed",
    "hardcoded one grade and every later curriculum needed a code change.",
    "",
    "Term keys are year-scoped here ('2026-2027-T01'), unlike legacy's bare",
    "'T1'. The new schema requires it: Term.key is globally unique, so 'T1'",
    "could only ever exist for one academic year.",
    "",
    "Every section below is named after the Prisma model it fills, and every",
    "field is named after a real column on that model. A key ending in 'Key'",
    "is a reference resolved to an id by the seed (Term.academicYearKey ->",
    "AcademicYear.id). tests/unit/seed-foundation-data.test.ts checks this",
    "against the generated Prisma schema, so a rename cannot drift silently."
  ],
  "AcademicYear": [
    {
      "key": "2026-2027",
      "startsOn": "2026-09-01",
      "endsOn": "2027-06-30",
      "isCurrent": true
    }
  ],
  "Term": [
    { "key": "2026-2027-T01", "academicYearKey": "2026-2027", "ordinal": 1, "name": "الفصل الدراسي الأول" },
    { "key": "2026-2027-T02", "academicYearKey": "2026-2027", "ordinal": 2, "name": "الفصل الدراسي الثاني" }
  ],
  "Grade": [
